## Decision: - Fedora S3 Uploaders: the current versioning of Fedora's uploaders means that files uploaded to the S3 version are
effectively being uploaded twice, which cannot be right. We have created the following test in the Fedora
admin function tool:
```php
function mountWithVersioning()
  {
  $files = getFilesForUpload();
  $repo = getRepoForUpload();
  $objects = getObjectsForRepo($repo, $files);

  for ($i=0; $i < count($objects); $i++)
  {
  $file = $objects[$i];

  // If there is a version of the object:
  if (fileVersion($file->version->getVersion()))
  {
  $fileVersion = $file->version;
  $fileStream = getRawFile($file);
  if (put($fileVersion->getAuthId(), $fileStream)
  {
  continue; // Continue to the next file in the loop
  }
  else
  {
  return false; // Return false if there's a problem uploading the file
  }
  }
  else
  {
  // The object is an "original" - upload it to Fedora by itself.
  if (put($file->version->getAuthId(), $fileStream))
  {
  continue; // Continue to the next file in the loop
  }
  else
  {
  return false; // Return false if there's a problem uploading the file
  }
  }
  }
  return true;
  }
```
  The result of the test is that, for each uploaded file, we get an upload result object containing information
  about whether the upload was successful, and any associated problem.

