## Decision: For all the new APIs this manual alias is used in a top-level manner. 

e.g. in a namespace with a huge amount of ops
```ts
Alias(MyAlias)
ops:{
	OpA: {
	  ...
	},
	OpB:{
	  ...
	}
	OpC:{
	  ...
	},
	MyAlias:{
	    ...
	}
	OpD:{
	  ...
	},
	OpE:{
	  ...
	}
	OpF:{
	  ...
	}
}
```
We can't and shouldn't alias to the `name` (e.g. `MyAlias`), which would not be convenient for the user as would have to be used twice.
Only Aliases for names, as in the example above are we using as aliases.
The above example already is not valid, and it's also in the context of an implementation, where the original comment may be present as a reference, while the alias would be used to be able to use the original name.
`Alias(MyAlias)` will now be `Alias(MyAlias)`.
For instance an "alias" from another namespace, can be used in this way:
```ts
Namespace("Alias")
alias = MyAlias
MyAlias(a, b) {
   ...
}
MyAlias = MyAlias
```

